-- title:
--   Idelic norm containing the unit ideles of an admissible modulus
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L/K$ Galois and $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ cyclic, let $n \neq 0$ be a natural number divisible by $[L:K] = \operatorname{finrank}_K L$, and let $\mathfrak f$ be an ideal of $\mathcal O_K$ that is admissible of degree $n$ for $L/K$, that is: $\mathfrak f \neq 0$ and, for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_K$ whose chosen prime above it in $\mathcal O_L$ has nontrivial inertia subgroup in $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$, $v^{e}$ divides $\mathfrak f$ with $e = 1 + \sum_{p \mid n} (v_p(n)+1)\,e(p\mathbb Z \mid v)$, the sum over the prime factors of $n$. Then there exists a group homomorphism $\mathrm{Nrm}$ from the idele units of $L$ to the idele units of $K$ such that: (1) whenever an idele unit $u$ of $L$ and $\alpha \in L^\times$ satisfy the adjuster condition for the extended modulus $\mathfrak f \mathcal O_L$ — at each prime $w$ of $L$ dividing $\mathfrak f\mathcal O_L$ the finite component of $u\alpha^{-1}$ at $w$ has valuation $1$ and $u_w\alpha^{-1} - 1$ has valuation at most $\exp(-n_w)$, $n_w$ the multiplicity of $w$ in $\mathfrak f\mathcal O_L$, and $u\alpha^{-1}$ has positive image under every real embedding of $L$ — then $\mathrm{Nrm}\,u$ and $N_{L/K}(\alpha)$ satisfy the corresponding adjuster condition for $\mathfrak f$ over $K$; (2) for every $u$, the fractional-ideal content of the finite part of $\mathrm{Nrm}\,u$ equals the image of the content of the finite part of $u$ under the relative norm map on fractional-ideal units, the latter being the ray symbol sending the prime unit at $w$ to the prime unit at $w \cap \mathcal O_K$ raised to the residue degree of $w$; (3) the subgroup of unit ideles of level $\mathfrak f$ (ideles of valuation $1$ at every finite place, congruent to $1$ modulo $\mathfrak f$ in the same valuation-theoretic sense, and positive at every real embedding) is contained in the range of $\mathrm{Nrm}$; and (4) $[L:K]$ divides the index of the subgroup generated by the principal ideles of $K$ together with the range of $\mathrm{Nrm}$.
--
--   This is the idelic first inequality of class field theory for a cyclic extension, packaged as the existence of a norm homomorphism with the four properties needed downstream: compatibility with adjusters and with contents, surjectivity onto the unit ideles of an admissible level, and divisibility of the norm-class index by the degree. It is used in the proof that the Artin symbol at an admissible modulus is surjective with kernel the norm ray subgroup.
